 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Where did the Ottoman Empire actually begin?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Right here. In Söğüt, a small town in northwest Türkiye."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "today",
   "date": "Today",
   "place": "Söğüt, Türkiye",
   "text": "Söğüt? I've never even heard of it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Most people haven't. It's about a hundred and fifty kilometres southeast of Istanbul."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "frontier",
   "date": "c. 1300",
   "place": "Bithynia",
   "text": "So why there?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Around 1300, this was a frontier. The Byzantine Empire held the west, and the Seljuk sultanate in the east was breaking apart into small principalities."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "One of them was led by a chief named Osman."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "osman",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.38,
     1.35
    ]
   },
   "text": "The word Ottoman comes from his name."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "dream",
   "text": "Is it true he dreamed the whole empire?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That's the legend. A chronicle written more than a century and a half later says he dreamed a tree grew from his body and spread over the world."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "bapheus",
   "text": "And what actually happened?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "date": "27 July 1302",
   "place": "Bapheus",
   "text": "In 1302, near Nicomedia, Osman's horsemen beat a Byzantine army at Bapheus. After that, fighters came from all over to join him."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "bursa",
   "date": "",
   "text": "Did he take any big cities?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. Byzantine walls were hard to break. But his son Orhan blockaded Bursa for years, and in 1326 it surrendered."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "orhan",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.42,
     1.25
    ]
   },
   "date": "6 April 1326",
   "place": "Bursa",
   "text": "Osman was buried there, and Bursa became the Ottomans' first great capital."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "borders",
   "date": "1326",
   "place": "Ottoman lands",
   "text": "So how big was it by then?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Still small. A strip of land from Söğüt to Bursa, squeezed between Byzantium and other Turkish principalities."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "timeline",
   "date": "",
   "text": "So how long did it all last?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Until 1922. More than six hundred years, from one small frontier town to three continents."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "osman2",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "Next time: how the Ottomans crossed into Europe. Like the video and follow History Sketches so you don't miss it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you'd like to know!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: into Europe",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ]
}